>
>I'm pretty sure the intrinsics are checked when you finish eating.
>Getting interupted shouldn't affect it.
>-- 
>Peter Snelling

You're right. Eating a monster can have different effects, some of which
happen when you take the first bite, and some when you finish eating. All the
intrinsics belong to the latter category, while a prime example of the former
is eating a lizard corpse to stop stoning (that's why you can go along with
just one lizard corpse : the cockatrice starts converting you to stone, you
start eating the lizard corpse immediately, you feel limber, then you are
attacked by the cockatrice again, and you end up with a nice partially
eaten lizard corpse). Having the intrinstics checked at the end of a meal
makes teleport control+teleport at will handy; you just teleport repeatedly
over that dragon's corpse until you are ready to eat it.

Vasilis Hatzivassiloglou.



